  "question": {
    "text": "The flat base of a hemisphere of radius a with no charge inside it lies in a horizontal plane. A uniform electric field $\\vec{E}$ is applied at an angle $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ with the vertical direction. The electric flux through the curved surface of the hemisphere is\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/_6cb2ByfNsdTFsVTNZ0WlwrpdayhcNoMkLxSS8NIbyw.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "aE7mm",
      "text": "\n$\\pi a^2 E$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MojXE",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi a^2 E}{\\sqrt{2}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "tlYPj",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi a^2 E}{2 \\sqrt{2}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fN1zz",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\left(\\pi+2 \\pi \\phi^2 E\\right.}{\\left(2 \\sqrt{2}{ }^2\\right)}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know that,\n$$\n\\phi=\\oint E \\cdot d S=E \\oint d S \\cos 45^{\\circ}\n$$\nIn case of hemisphere\n$$\n\\phi_{\\text {curved }}=\\phi_{\\text {circular }}\n$$\nTherefore, $\\phi_{\\text {curved }}=E \\pi a^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{E \\pi a^2}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
    "image": null
  },
